package com.wjx.touhou_aifun.chat.agent;

/** Stable action guidance belongs in the cacheable policy, not every mutable checkpoint. */
public final class AgentTaskInstructions {
    private AgentTaskInstructions() { }
    public static final String DECISION_POLICY="## Typed decision execution\n"
            +"An independent JEV/Decider service evaluates finite choices, not free-text plans. After fresh observations, register the FULL completion contract and a complete action_steps plan in ONE standalone update_task_plan call. Do not combine an executable plan with other actions in that batch. Include every additional owner requirement as a step. One fixed alternative executes directly; multiple alternatives and omitted enum/boolean parameters use the decision service. Unknown required free-text parameters or visual operations return to you for planning. Never build text by chaining choices.\n"
            +"The ordinary ordered-batch guidance applies only to plans without action_steps; action_steps must be submitted alone. Use $live.session_id and $live.revision for the currently open GUI. For the Nth atomic completion condition, transfer arguments may bind slot=$live.from_slot_N, to_slot=$live.to_slot_N, count=$live.transfer_count_N; code calculates remaining amounts and legal current slots. Use an until predicate for repeated transfers, so the step stops only when its actual required quantity has been delivered. Use skip_if on opening/preparation steps already made unnecessary by verified completion; until would repeat that preparation instead of advancing. Use $live bindings instead of saving predicted/stale session or slot ids. Fixed targets must come from the owner's scope and fresh observations. Optional target_binding selects only already observed block/container/entity candidates by description and kind, binding $target.x/y/z/registry_id/entity_id/entity_uuid in arguments; never invent coordinates or entity identity.\n"
            +"Startup may select a complete common follow/sit/schedule/work-mode/receive/deliver template without an execution LLM call. Extra requirements, ambiguity, amended scope or unsupported quantities return to you for full planning. Work-mode selection does not prove that work was completed. All typed steps and the FULL completion contract must pass server verification before automatic completion. maid_state verifies follow/sit/schedule/work_task; eat_food verifies actual consumed servings and optional finished. Known stale menus or lost sessions may refresh/reopen the same authorized target; ambiguous physical failures select a finite recovery strategy. Recovery is bounded to two attempts per step and always preserves committed facts and remaining quantities. Unsafe one-off mutations, unknown bindings, unsupported failures or uncertainty return to the execution LLM. Do not replay committed facts or weaken the completion contract.\n";
    public static final String POLICY = "## AIFun action execution rules\n"
            + "Match the owner's requested sources and number of containers. Scans may include unrelated neighbouring chests or repeated category labels; do not inspect or collect all candidates automatically. If multiple groups fit and the requested sources cannot be distinguished, ask the owner and pause rather than broadening the goal." + "\n"
            + "Tool schemas are selected automatically for the current observation, planning, execution or verification stage. Invoke tools present in the request directly; do not load group:gui before normal container work. In an open planning menu, put update_task_plan defining completion BEFORE the first GUI mutation in the SAME ordered batch when the observed slots are already sufficient. If an additional owner requirement needs a missing tool, load its exact id. A verification-stage menu does not declare the task completed or discard additional owner requirements." + "\n"
            + "Observe the current signs/containers and inventory, then call update_task_plan with completion covering EVERY requested item, quantity and source/destination. For 'take everything' with unknown amounts, use ONE inspect_containers(targets) call for all observed container positions; use its counts to define the full contract and operate the still-open active_gui first. If the owner already specified exact quantities/containers, register them without a separate inspection tour. GUI inspection is allowed; gui_action/gui_batch/wait_gui item mutations or collection are blocked until this condition is defined. Do not invent dummy conditions or assume success from a sentence." + "\n"
            + "Use these current server facts to check all explicit user requirements. On the FINAL gui_action/gui_batch that will satisfy ALL owner requirements, set complete_task=true: the tool performs actual actions, closes/settles the menu and requests runtime verification in this same call, with no final model report round. For intermediate transfers set close_after=true when done with that menu, and optionally put the next open_gui in the SAME ordered tool batch. Do not close a menu in a separate model turn. When completion cannot be declared with the last GUI action (e.g. additional arrival), call update_task_plan with complete=true at the last step after satisfying it. Do not reopen containers solely to reconfirm quantities or emptiness already covered by complete live source_checks. Unknown/unloaded/double-container coverage still requires observation. Verified predicates do not replace additional user requirements." + "\n";
}
